      <details>
        <summary>How much does fitness UGC cost?</summary>
        <div class="ans">
          <p>Our fitness UGC packages start at $500 for 10 video assets and scale based on volume, complexity, and creator tier. Standard packages include script writing, creator matching, filming, editing, and delivery in multiple platform formats. Transformation or series content that requires filming over multiple weeks costs more due to the extended creator engagement. We also offer monthly retainer packages for brands that need a continuous flow of fresh creative — these typically range from $1,500 to $5,000 per month depending on asset volume and creator caliber. Every package includes 3-5 hook variants per concept, platform-native formatting, and burned-in captions at no extra charge.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What types of fitness creators do you work with?</summary>
        <div class="ans">
          <p>Our creator roster spans the full fitness spectrum: powerlifters, bodybuilders, CrossFit athletes, yoga instructors, marathon runners, casual gym-goers, personal trainers, nutritionists, and wellness-focused lifestyle creators. We match creators based on your product category, target demographic, and brand tone. If you sell a mass-market protein powder, we might pair you with relatable everyday gym-goers. If you sell a premium pre-workout for serious athletes, we source creators with competitive training backgrounds and visible credentials. We also have creators who specialize in specific content formats — some excel at talking-head testimonials, others at workout integration footage, and others at transformation storytelling. Geography, language, and demographic diversity are all part of the matching process.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How fast can we get fitness UGC content?</summary>
        <div class="ans">
          <p>Standard turnaround for a batch of fitness UGC is 7 business days from brief approval to final delivery. This includes creator matching (1-2 days), filming (2-3 days), and editing with revisions (2-3 days). Rush delivery in 4-5 days is available for an additional fee. The exception is transformation or progress content, which inherently requires a multi-week filming period — typically 2-4 weeks depending on the narrative arc. For brands on a monthly retainer, we establish a rolling production schedule so new assets land every week without requiring a new brief each time. If you are launching a new product or running a time-sensitive campaign, let us know upfront and we will prioritize accordingly.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can we use the UGC content for paid ads?</summary>
        <div class="ans">
          <p>Yes — every piece of content we produce comes with full paid media usage rights. You can run it as sponsored content on Meta (Facebook and Instagram), TikTok, YouTube, Pinterest, Snapchat, and any other paid platform without additional licensing fees. Usage rights are perpetual unless otherwise specified in the contract. We also support whitelisting and Spark Ads setups where the ad runs from the creator's own account, which typically delivers 15-30% lower CPMs due to the native appearance. If you need creator account access for Partnership Ads on Meta or Spark Ads on TikTok, we coordinate that directly with the creator so your media buyer gets seamless access. All content is delivered as high-resolution files suitable for both organic posting and paid amplification.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do you handle supplement advertising compliance?</summary>
        <div class="ans">
          <p>Yes, we build FTC and FDA compliance into every fitness and supplement brief from the start. Our process includes a pre-approved claims list developed with your team, a restricted phrases guide for creators, and an internal review step before any content goes live. We ensure creators avoid disease claims, unsubstantiated health claims, and before-and-after implications that could trigger regulatory scrutiny. We also add required disclaimers and disclosures — including FTC-mandated ad disclosures for paid partnerships — to all content. While we are not a legal compliance firm and recommend brands have their legal team review final assets for high-stakes campaigns, our built-in guardrails prevent the vast majority of compliance issues before they reach the review stage. We stay current on platform-specific policies for health and supplement advertising on Meta, TikTok, and Google.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

